8,Austronesian Soundscapes,https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/austronesian-soundscapes/8B714F18DC010F5F8E4997353C4B18BA,"Drawing together contemporary cultural studies and musical analysis, Austronesian Soundscapes will fill this research gap, offering a comprehensive analysis of traditional and contemporary Austronesian music and, at the same time, investigating how music reflects the challenges that Austronesian cultures face in this age of globalization.",Idaté,Austronesian
9,Austronesian Music - Music genre - Rate Your Music,https://rateyourmusic.com/genre/austronesian-music/,"Using a zither in the form of a bamboo pipe rounded by strings, called sasando/sasandu/valiha/kolibit as an accompaniment of narrative songs; also other corresponding traditions using different instruments (Sundanese pantun, dayak sape).Austronesian music nowadays refers to the ongoing evolution and fusion of various cultural influences from foreign and neighbouring cultures.",Idaté,Austronesian
